urn it off  giving you  no hints whatsoever including disabling  the story mission menu  the story opportunities still exist but  they're no longer presented as obvious  objectives  they fade into the background as another  small part of the grand clockwork system  that makes up these levels and it's a  lot of fun to play this way  in fact if you've already played all the  way through hitman 3 you've had an  opportunity to try this for yourself  with the berlin mission  which has no handler and therefore no  story missions  however that mission still has scripted  moments that are absolutely  story like missions just without calling  them that and that's basically what  you're getting throughout the entire  experience  if you choose to turn mission story  guidance off  you'll find yourself soaking up  information eavesdropping on npcs  and parsing out any useful details you  can exploit  hot tip if you have subtitles on any  dialogue that shows up  usually contains a clue that can  potentially help you in some way  they are also smartly written to provide  you with all the information you need  for example in sapienza if you walk into  this hair salon  you'll overhear a conversation where an  employee is talking about his private  detective brother who is in town on a  case for francesca desantes  who is one of our targets naturally this  leads you to the conclusion that this pi  could help you get closer to her  and conveniently they mention where to  find him sleeping on a bench  a few blocks away so you explore the  surrounding area and  lo and behold there he is you can wake  him up with the radio  and then listen to his phone  conversation with francesca  where he plans to meet her by the pier  at which point  you might get the clever idea to knock  out the pi  and pretend to be him at the meeting now  if you were to follow  the guided instructions it still leads  to the same result  but that's just it you're following  instructions  you don't get that moment w